### Re-run at the merged head: the committed budget driver, with its exhaustion repaired

The review's P2 on `scripts/proof-cli-stream-turn-budget.ts:211-216` is correct. `measureClaudeToolResultMessage` discounts a tool-result payload to `max(32, rawLine.length - payloadChars)`, and a partial text delta is charged its text plus a fixed envelope, so the old fixture's 96,000-character tool-result bodies charged roughly 230 characters per ~96 KiB iteration. The loop stopped on its 32 MiB wire cap with well under 8 MiB charged and `assertBudgetSpent` threw before the first retention scenario — every post-budget assertion in the file was unreachable. Both committed drivers now exhaust with chargeable ordinary assistant records (64 KiB of text per frame, ~128 frames, far below the 20,000-line odometer) and verify exhaustion before measuring.

